# ---- 11. Statement-level call rewrites (Java name -> SLeeLa call).
call System.out.println print($args)
call array.length arrayLength($recv)

# ---- 12. Constructs the converter refuses, with the reason it states.
unsupported float float arithmetic rounds to IEEE binary32 at every step; SLeeLa has no binary32 operator set, so equivalence cannot be guaranteed
unsupported lambda lambdas need the linear lowering of lib/java/jdk-28/LOWERING.md (design draft, not implemented in the converter)
unsupported methodref method references need the linear lowering of lib/java/jdk-28/LOWERING.md
unsupported synchronized synchronized blocks have no SLeeLa form
unsupported enum enum declarations are listed in SLEELA.syntax 43.5 as not supported
unsupported incr-expr ++/-- of a floating point value used as a value cannot recover the old value exactly
unsupported assign-expr an assignment inside a construct the converter cannot hoist or sequence
unsupported switch-expr a switch expression must start the expression of a declaration, assignment, return or expression statement; type patterns and case null are not converted
unsupported string-static String is a keyword type in SLeeLa, so String.valueOf / String.format / String.join cannot be called as static members yet
unsupported nested nested/inner/anonymous types are not converted yet
unsupported untyped operand type cannot be determined, so the Java operator semantics cannot be selected
unsupported init-block a static initializer block, or an initializer block outside an ordinary class, is not converted yet; instance initializer blocks are converted
unsupported member-annotation an annotation type or annotation member declaration is not converted
unsupported object-method a java.lang.Object method (equals, hashCode, getClass ...) on a user type that does not declare it is not converted yet
